            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A DC/DC power converter 100 has an input terminal 111, an output terminal 112, and a ground terminal 113. The DC/DC power converter 100 comprises two capacitors 121, 122 connected in series between the output terminal 112 and the ground terminal 113, a boost converter 130 having a first boost converter terminal 131 connected to the input terminal 111, a second boost converter terminal 132 connected to the output terminal 112, and a third boost converter terminal 133 connected to a connection point 123 between the capacitors 121, 122, and a step-up converter 140 having a first step-up converter terminal 141 connected to the ground terminal 113, a second step-up converter terminal 142 connected to the output terminal 112, and a third step-up converter terminal 143 connected to the connection point 123.</p>
            </abstract>
